{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_bdrk_aek2wk3id6btdfhgodovz2kspod5xvjnhisijwzajckbib7wwela","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All six screens are built in 03 · Workspace and linked as a clickable prototype. I took a screenshot of every screen, fixed what looked wrong (a message card that overflowed, cut-off timeline phase names, a chat bubble that wrapped too narrow, a clipped schedule card) and checked them again. The account was confirmed as zuohaosheng@tetras.ai, and I only read the reference pages (00, 01, 02, 04), never edited them.\n\n**File:** https://www.figma.com/design/VFR5xWR7hrm3DOj4Y7qX0O/\n**03 · Workspace page ID:** `8:2`\n\n| Screen | ID |\n|---|---|\n| 01_Dashboard | `12:176` |\n| 02_Timeline | `14:415` |\n| 03_Task_Board | `18:672` |\n| 04_Files | `19:1155` |\n| 05_Settings | `21:1406` |\n| 06_Messages | `23:1529` |\n\n**Prototype (34 click links):**\n- On all 6 screens, each sidebar icon opens its screen: Dashboard → 01, Timeline → 02, Task → 03, Settings → 05, Messages → 06, Files → 04. That's 30 links. The current screen's own icon has no link.\n- On 01_Dashboard, all 4 message rows open 06_Messages.\n- The flow starts on 01_Dashboard (\"OCTOM · Main flow\").\n- The other controls are visual only, as the brief says (\"entry only\").\n\n**Components** (section \"Components · OCTOM\", `10:2`):\n- **Navigation:** nav item (6 icons × Default / Hover / Current), sidebar (one version per current page), top bar with a notification count of 2, round crop of the current-user photo.\n- **Shared controls:** Secondary, Soft and Primary-with-icon buttons, icon buttons, tags (Design, Research, Planning, Content), period tabs, settings tabs (Default / Hover / Current).\n- **Text fields:** I made Focused, With Icon and Disabled versions from the given Text Field. The given Button and Text Field themselves are used on the screens.\n- **Screen items:** stat card, task row, message row (Default / Hover), gantt bar (5 colors), phase row, day cell (Default / Today), task card (switches for cover, checklist, comments and files), column header, chat bubbles and voice message, folder card, file row, storage item, conversation item (Default / Current / Typing, with Unread and Online switches), message bubble, day divider, attachment row, member row, upload area.\n- **Design system frame** (`25:1694`): colors, type scale, corner radii, spacing and shadows, plus local color and text styles. Everything uses DM Sans and the brand color #5051F9, with photos, avatars and icons from 04 · Media.\n\n**Limitations and choices you should know about:**\n- **Day scale:** the brief says \"S 04 … S 21\", so the last day is labelled S. In the real June 2022 calendar, the 21st is a Tuesday.\n- **Progress bars:** Figma ignored resizing layers inside component copies here. I show progress with a two-color hard-stop fill instead. The bars look correct, but the percentage is set in the fill, not by a bar width you can drag.\n- **Text I added** that isn't in the brief's data: \"Project Phases\", \"Pinned\", \"Used of total storage\", the subtitle \"Dristin Watson · Product Designer\", and Mon–Sun labels on the activity chart.\n- **Task Done chart:** it has no legend for its two lines, because the brief doesn't name the series.\n- **Hover states:** they exist as component versions but aren't wired as hover interactions in the prototype."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26,"cache_creation_input_tokens":179451,"cache_read_input_tokens":7706,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":179451,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17a8062a-11f9-422a-8d16-9eb105e98fb8","uuid":"56cbae34-aa1e-4472-9ac0-483259c6490d","timestamp":"2026-11-01T21:22:48.389Z"}
